    <statement><p>Simplify the expression
<me>3 \sqrt[3]{4} \left( 4 \sqrt[3]{16} + 4 \sqrt[3]{7} \right)</me>
and express your answer in the simplest radical form <m>A+ B \sqrt[3]{C},</m> where <m>A,</m> <m>B,</m> and <m>C</m> are integers.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>A =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>, <m>B =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/>, and <m>C =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4\cdot 3\cdot 4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>3\cdot 4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7\cdot 4</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
